[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 1: Identifying $\rho_1$ as the cyclotomic character.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe natural action of $G_\mathbb{Q}$ on $\widehat{\mathbb{Z}}$ arises from the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mGalois action on roots of unity. Consider the Tate module of the group of all [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mroots of unity:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$T(\mu_\infty) = \varprojlim_{n} \mu_n$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhere the transition map $\mu_{mn} \to \mu_n$ is $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^m$. As a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mprofinite abelian group, $T(\mu_\infty) \cong \widehat{\mathbb{Z}}$ (non-[0m
